# AI git policy

## Branches

- **Never** develop or commit product work directly on `main` / `master`.
- Use: `agent/<short-topic>`, `feature/<short-topic>`, or `experiment/<id-slug>`.
- Cut the branch before implementing a TASK_QUEUE item when currently on `main`.

## Commits

- One logical task (TASK_QUEUE id) → one commit, or a small focused stack.
- Prefer conventional commits: `feat`, `fix`, `chore`, `docs`, `refactor`, `test`.
- Message explains **why**; reference experiment/task ids when useful.
- Do not commit: `Library/`, `Temp/`, `Logs/`, secrets, `artifacts/ai/` logs, IDE junk.
- Do not commit unless the user/workflow allows commits for this autonomy level; still prepare a clean diff.

## Push / PR / main

- No `--force` to `main`/`master`. Warn if asked.
- Level 2: commit locally; ask before push.
- Level 3: push `agent/*` / `feature/*` and open a PR; do not merge unless Level 4 granted.
- Remote: `origin` → `https://github.com/Nadomas/ranalog-ra2.git` when configured.

## After task complete

- Update `docs/ai/TASK_QUEUE.md` in the same change set when practical.
- Leave the working tree ready for the next open task on the same or a fresh `agent/*` branch.
